course: dictionary
lesson: 8312
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Rob usually means to take something from someone in a wrong way. «The thief tried to rob the bank at night.» The clues are thief and bank, so rob means to steal.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The injury robbed her of the win.» Nobody took a bag of money here. Robbed of means someone lost something good they should have had, so the injury took away her chance to win.
explain: Sometimes rob is a name. «There are not enough chairs, Uncle Rob is missing because of a row.» Rob here is a short name for Robert, a person, and it starts with a capital letter. The capital letter and the rest of the sentence are your clues.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If "steal" still makes sense, you have probably got it. If it sounds silly, read the words around it again.
fact: Rob is a verb (rob, robs, robbed, robbing) and also a short name for Robert.
fact: «Rob» means to take money or things from a person or place in a wrong way, often by force or threats.
fact: To rob someone of something means to take away something good they should have.
fact: «Daylight robbery» is an informal phrase meaning the price is far too high.
fact: Keep your valuables safe, and tell a grown-up straight away if something is stolen.
exercise: «The thief tried to rob the bank at night.» What does rob mean here? | To count coins for fun | *To take money or things in a wrong way | To paint a bank in bright colours | To sit down and wait
exercise: «The injury robbed her of the win.» What does robbed of mean here? | *Took away something good she should have had | Made her run faster | Gave her a prize | Told her a joke
exercise: Chen says, «That price is daylight robbery!» What does he mean? | *The price is far too high | It is very sunny outside | He wants a longer day | The shop is being robbed right now
test: «Uncle Rob is missing because of a row.» Is Rob a person's name here? | No, it means a dress in French | No, it is a type of boat | *Yes, a short name for Robert | No, it means to take something
test: «Being mugged means being robbed in the street.» What should you do if this happens? | Chase the robber on your own | Wait for it to happen again | Keep it a secret forever | *Tell a parent and the police
exam: Jayden says rob always means steal. Is he right? | No, rob means to paint | Yes, rob is only ever a verb | *No, rob can also mean to take away something good someone should have, or be a name | Yes, rob only ever means steal
